WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.808
The school assigned these readings because a patient is more than a medication calculation. You need to understand what was ordered, what the patient actually took, how breathing can fail and whether your proposed care is lawful and within your role.
学校指定这些阅读，是因为患者不只是一道药算。你要理解医嘱、患者实际服用、呼吸如何失败，以及拟议照护是否合法且在自己角色内。

00:00:14.808 --> 00:00:29.448
The paired reading below follows the assigned page spans in the available candidate books. It teaches the narrative domains and identifies incorrect or jurisdiction-specific statements rather than reproducing every textbook sentence.
下方中英阅读按现有候选书的指定页段展开，教授正文领域，并指出错误或司法地区特定陈述，不是逐句复制教材。

00:00:29.448 --> 00:00:42.792
This lecture links those domains to the Week Two airway and medication stations. The practical airway sequence remains in its own lesson so that a mental-health discussion never delays an effective breath.
这堂把阅读连到第2周气道及用药站。实际气道顺序保留在专门课中，精神健康讨论不能延误一次有效通气。

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:56.016
Use the source notes for unresolved edition and interactive material. A detailed reading guide is useful learning content, but it is not evidence that an unrecovered school activity has been completed.
版本及互动材料未解决处请看来源说明。详细讲解是实际学习内容，却不证明未取得的学校活动已经完成。

00:00:56.016 --> 00:01:10.512
Begin with the patient and the reason for treatment. An amount can be mathematically correct while the indication is wrong or a contraindication makes it unsafe. Explain what improvement you expect and what harm you are looking for.
先看患者及治疗理由。药量可数学正确，适应证却错，或有禁忌而不安全。应解释预期改善及需找的伤害。

00:01:10.512 --> 00:01:25.896
Verification includes the real package, formulation, expiry and integrity as well as the order. Similar brand names, combination products and a changed tablet strength can create an error before anyone touches a syringe.
核实包括真实包装、剂型、效期、完整性及医嘱。近似商品名、复方或片量变化，可在动针筒前就造成错误。

00:01:25.896 --> 00:01:40.944
Delivery means the medicine actually reaches the appropriate place at the appropriate rate. A leaking IV, an uncoordinated inhaler or swallowed sublingual tablet can change delivery even when the prepared amount was correct.
给入是药物真正以适当速度到适当位置。静脉漏液、吸入器不协调或把舌下药吞下，即使准备量正确，也会改变送入。

00:01:40.944 --> 00:01:54.480
Finish with the patient again. Record what happened, including partial or failed delivery, and reassess the effect. Reciting a list of rights is preparation for that process, not a substitute for carrying it out.
最后再回患者：记录实际经过，包括部分或失败给入，并复评效果。背正确原则是为流程准备，不能代替执行。

00:01:54.480 --> 00:02:10.008
A usable order identifies the person, drug, amount, route and timing, with relevant concentration, weight, limits and indication. A missing route is not repaired by choosing whichever route seems fastest.
可执行医嘱明确患者、药物、药量、途径及时间，并有相关浓度、体重、限制及适应证。缺途径不能靠挑看似最快的补上。

00:02:10.008 --> 00:02:24.816
An as-needed order still has a reason and safe boundaries. A stat order changes urgency, not the obligation to check. Titration requires a defined target, increments and reassessment under actual authority.
按需医嘱仍有理由及安全边界；立即医嘱改变紧急度，不取消核查。滴定需要真实权限下规定目标、增量及复评。

00:02:24.816 --> 00:02:38.088
Do not silently translate twice daily into every twelve hours or three times daily into every eight hours. Those may be different schedules; use the actual instruction and resolve uncertainty.
不能悄悄把一天两次变成每12小时，或一天三次变每8小时，它们可不同。须用真实指示并解决不确定。

00:02:38.088 --> 00:02:50.376
For a verbal order, read back the complete medicine, units, route and timing and obtain confirmation according to policy. Guessing is not made safer by saying the scene was busy.
口头医嘱应回读完整药、单位、途径及时间，按政策取得确认。场面繁忙不能让猜测变安全。

00:02:50.376 --> 00:03:05.880
The actual formulation determines how the medicine is prepared and absorbed. Crushing an enteric-coated or modified-release product can change its intended function; swallowing trouble needs an appropriate plan, not automatic crushing.
真实剂型决定准备及吸收。压碎肠溶或缓释可改变设计功能；吞咽问题需合适方案，不是自动压碎。

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:21.024
A sublingual or buccal product uses mucosal delivery. A swallowed dose is not necessarily equivalent. Rectal, vaginal, topical and transdermal routes also need their own product, consent and scope checks.
舌下或颊用产品经黏膜送入，吞下不一定等效。直肠、阴道、外用及经皮也各需产品、同意及范围核查。

00:03:21.024 --> 00:03:35.760
For nasal medication, follow the actual device. Do not prime a sealed emergency naloxone or glucagon spray by wasting part of its dose. The dead-space arithmetic for a syringe atomizer is a separate process.
鼻药按真实装置，不能为了预喷而浪费密封急救纳洛酮或胰高血糖素。注射器雾化的死腔算法是另一过程。

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:50.976
IV medicine enters the circulation without an absorption step, but target effects can still take time. Check patency, compatibility, rate and residual tubing volume rather than assuming a pushed syringe proves successful treatment.
静脉药无需吸收即入循环，但靶效仍可需时。应核通畅、相容性、速度及管内残量，不能认为推空针筒就证明治疗成功。

00:03:50.976 --> 00:04:05.808
A pressurized metered-dose inhaler uses propellant. A nebulizer may be driven by compressed gas or electricity depending on the system. Do not repeat the candidate text's implication that every inhaler needs electrical power.
加压定量吸入器靠推进剂；雾化器按系统可气驱或电驱。不能重复候选教材暗示所有吸入器需电力的说法。

00:04:05.808 --> 00:04:20.664
Select and coordinate the actual spacer or mask with the person's breathing. A severely distressed patient may be unable to perform an ideal prolonged breath-hold, and a poorly sealed interface can waste the prepared dose.
须选择并协调真实储雾罐或面罩与患者呼吸。严重窘迫者可能无法理想长屏气，密封不良也可浪费准备量。

00:04:20.664 --> 00:04:34.368
Count what was actually administered, then assess whether the person is moving air. A fading wheeze with reduced air entry and exhaustion is not reassuring merely because the device ran for the expected time.
记录实际给入，再看是否真正有气流。哮鸣变弱但气流少且疲竭，不会因装置已运行规定时间就令人放心。

00:04:34.368 --> 00:04:46.416
If effective breaths are failing, provide ventilatory support and reassess the pathway. Do not continue counting bronchodilator puffs while ignoring a patient who needs assisted ventilation.
有效呼吸失败时，应支持通气并重评路径，不能继续数支扩喷数却忽略需要辅助通气的患者。

00:04:46.416 --> 00:05:00.312
Reassessment begins during administration when immediate harm is possible. A textbook five-to-fifteen-minute interval is not permission to wait through apnea, anaphylaxis or a suddenly painful swollen IV site.
可能有即时伤害时，给药中就开始复评。教材5至15分钟间隔，不允许面对呼吸停止、过敏性休克或静脉点骤痛肿胀仍等待。

00:05:00.312 --> 00:05:15.360
Record the product, actual amount, route, relevant site, time, reason, response and complication. If half the prepared medicine leaked or delivery stopped, do not chart the whole planned dose as administered.
应记产品、实际药量、途径、相关部位、时间、理由、反应及并发症。准备的一半漏掉或给入中止，不能把全部计划量记为已给。

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:28.080
An incident report and a patient care record have different purposes. Complete the required process without falsifying, deleting an important finding or pre-charting treatment that has not happened.
事件报告及患者记录目的不同。须完成要求，但不能造假、删重要发现或提前记尚未发生的治疗。

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:42.768
After an error, first protect and assess the patient and get appropriate assistance. Honest communication and system learning follow; hiding an error prevents both effective rescue and prevention of the next one.
出错先保护评估患者并取得适当协助，再诚实沟通及系统学习；隐瞒会阻碍有效补救及预防下次。

00:05:42.768 --> 00:05:57.264
Explain the proposed care, important benefits and risks, alternatives and the consequences of declining. Check understanding, not just whether a form has a signature. A patient may understand and still make a choice you dislike.
应解释拟议照护、重要收益风险、替代及拒绝后果，核理解而非只看签名。患者可以理解，却作出你不喜欢的选择。

00:05:57.264 --> 00:06:10.896
Language difference, deafness, a psychiatric diagnosis or an unusual appearance does not alone prove incapacity. Use appropriate communication support and assess the actual decision the person is making.
语言不同、耳聋、精神科诊断或外观特别，单独都不证明无能力。应提供沟通支持并评估患者正在作的具体决定。

00:06:10.896 --> 00:06:24.456
Urgency does not erase a capable refusal. If the person cannot participate, establish the actual emergency and legal pathway rather than using implied consent as an unlimited permission label.
紧急不会抹掉有能力拒绝。患者不能参与时，要建立真实紧急情况及法律路径，不能用默示同意当无限许可标签。

00:06:24.456 --> 00:06:39.672
After oxygenation, ventilation, glucose or poisoning improves, revisit capacity and the explanation. Naloxone response alone does not establish an informed refusal or remove the need for the current refusal process.
氧合、通气、血糖或中毒改善后，应重评能力及解释。纳洛酮有反应本身不证明拒绝已知情，也不取消当前拒绝流程。

00:06:39.672 --> 00:06:56.160
The assigned legal reading uses U.S. Nurse Practice Acts, state boards, HIPAA and other U.S. structures. Learn the distinctions between law, regulation, licence and policy without copying those structures as BC paramedic legislation.
指定法律阅读用美国护理执业法、州委员会、HIPAA等。应学法律、规章、执照及政策的区别，但不把这些结构抄成BC急救员法律。

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:10.296
A course certificate, an employer instruction and a textbook procedure do not independently create every practice permission. Check the actual licence, required education, service conditions and current procedure.
结课证、雇主指示及教材步骤，都不能独立创造全部权限。须核真实执照、必需教育、机构条件及当前规程。

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:27.240
Likewise, neither a diagnosis nor a difficult interaction grants a blanket power to restrain or transport someone involuntarily. Use actual legal authority and the least restrictive appropriate approach, with reassessment and consultation.
诊断或难沟通也不提供全面约束或非自愿转运权力。须有真实法律权限，使用最低限制的适当方式，伴复评及咨询。

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:43.296
Keep evidence factual: observations, timing, what was said, options, reasoning, consultations and actual care. An adverse outcome alone does not prove negligence, and a confident note cannot repair an unsafe action.
证据应客观：观察、时间、原话、选择、理由、咨询及实际照护。结局不良本身不证明过失，自信的记录也不能修复不安全行为。

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:54.360
Ask for the exact product and formulation rather than accepting only a familiar brand name. Inspect the package when available and compare the usual strength with the recent refill.
要问准确产品剂型，不能只接受熟悉品牌。可得时看包装，比较平时含量与最近续药。

00:07:54.360 --> 00:08:06.288
Explore timing, missed doses and extra doses without blame. A person may be trying to follow instructions but misunderstand a changed tablet strength or dosing device.
不责备地了解时序、漏服及多服。患者可能正努力照指示，却误解改变的片量或量药装置。

00:08:06.288 --> 00:08:19.416
Ask about alcohol, supplements, pain and cold medicines and other substances. A prescribed sedative combined with an opioid may explain respiratory depression better than either medication name alone.
应问酒精、补充品、止痛感冒药及其他物质。处方镇静药加阿片，比单一药名更可解释呼吸抑制。

00:08:19.416 --> 00:08:32.112
Do not force every finding into the psychiatric history. Hypoglycemia, infection, trauma and medication toxicity remain possible in a person with a mental-health diagnosis.
不能把所有发现硬塞精神病史。有精神健康诊断者仍可能低血糖、感染、创伤或药物毒性。

00:08:32.112 --> 00:08:45.552
Antipsychotic medications differ in their dopamine and serotonin effects. Some movement reactions follow treatment and can be mistaken for psychiatric deterioration if the exposure timeline is ignored.
抗精神病药的多巴胺与血清素作用不同。部分治疗后运动反应，若忽略用药时序，会被误为精神病恶化。

00:08:45.552 --> 00:08:59.976
Acute dystonia involves sustained abnormal contractions. Neck, tongue or airway involvement requires urgent assessment. Do not merely tell the person to calm down or assume every unusual posture is deliberate.
急性肌张力障碍涉及持续异常收缩，颈、舌或气道受累须急评。不能只叫冷静，或认为每种怪姿势都是故意。

00:08:59.976 --> 00:09:14.424
Akathisia can cause intense inner restlessness, while drug-induced parkinsonism produces a different pattern of slowness and rigidity. Tardive dyskinesia is another pattern, not an interchangeable name for all of them.
静坐不能可有强烈内在不安，药源帕金森则是迟缓僵硬的另一模式；迟发运动障碍又不同，不能互换名字。

00:09:14.424 --> 00:09:32.088
Ask about new treatment, dose changes and symptom onset; assess ABCs and distress and communicate the suspected medication relationship. Specific reversal treatment requires the appropriate authorized pathway, not a guessed extra drug.
应问新治疗、改量及发作时间，评ABC与痛苦，并交代疑用药关联。具体逆转需适当获准路径，不是猜一种额外药。

00:09:32.088 --> 00:09:47.976
Neuroleptic malignant syndrome is an emergency concern with relevant exposure and a combination of altered awareness, marked rigidity, temperature elevation and autonomic instability. It is not simply a mild extrapyramidal effect.
相关暴露后，意识改变、明显强直、升温及自主神经不稳组合提示恶性综合征急症，不能只当轻微锥体外系反应。

00:09:47.976 --> 00:10:03.816
Serotonergic toxicity has a different medication context and important neuromuscular findings such as clonus or hyperreflexia. Real presentations can overlap; do not diagnose either from one temperature or movement alone.
血清素毒性有不同药物背景，阵挛或反射亢进等神经肌肉发现重要；真实表现可交叉，不能只凭一次温度或动作确诊任一种。

00:10:03.816 --> 00:10:18.456
An initially alert overdose patient can still deteriorate. Tricyclic medicines can produce serious cardiac and neurologic toxicity, and modified-release bupropion can produce delayed seizures and serious effects.
过量患者起初清醒仍可恶化。三环类可严重心脏神经毒性，缓释安非他酮可延迟抽搐及严重后果。

00:10:18.456 --> 00:10:33.144
Preserve airway and breathing support, obtain the appropriate assistance and convey the exposure, amount uncertainty, formulation and time course. Do not substitute a psychiatric label for an acute poisoning assessment.
须保气道呼吸支持、取得适当协助，并交代暴露、量不确定、剂型及时程，不能以精神标签替代急性中毒评估。

00:10:33.144 --> 00:10:45.960
Lithium has a narrow safety margin and important renal handling. Intercurrent illness, fluid and sodium changes and interacting medicines can change risk even when the prescription is not new.
锂安全余地窄且重要依赖肾处理。即使非新处方，合并疾病、水钠变化及相互作用也可改变风险。

00:10:45.960 --> 00:11:03.360
Vomiting, diarrhea, tremor, poor coordination, slurred speech and confusion deserve attention in the right context. Do not dismiss the combination as a harmless side effect or wait for an exact laboratory number before recognizing possible toxicity.
相关背景下，呕吐、腹泻、震颤、协调差、言语含糊及混乱需注意。不能把组合当无害副作用，也不能等特定化验数才考虑毒性。

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:16.560
For a changed refill, calculate from the actual old and new labels rather than tablet count alone. Carry the packaging or reliable medication list into the handover and document the uncertainty honestly.
续药有变化时，须按新旧真实标签算，不只看片数。交接带包装或可靠清单，并如实记录不确定。

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:29.832
The role here is recognition, assessment and appropriate escalation. This lesson does not prescribe a home dose change, fluid-and-salt rescue plan or a psychiatric medication substitution.
此处角色是辨认、评估及适当升级，不开家庭改量、水盐补救或精神药替换方案。

00:11:29.832 --> 00:11:45.672
Benzodiazepines enhance inhibitory GABA-A function. Combined with opioids, alcohol or other depressants, the concern includes impaired airway protection and inadequate ventilation, not only whether the person looks sleepy.
苯二氮䓬增强抑制性GABA-A功能，与阿片、酒精或其他抑制物合用时，要担心气道保护及通气不足，不只是看起来困。

00:11:45.672 --> 00:11:59.136
Assess rate and effective depth, chest movement, air entry, awareness and circulation. Supplemental oxygen can improve saturation while carbon dioxide clearance remains inadequate.
须评次数及有效深度、胸动、气流、意识及循环。补氧可改善饱和度，CO2清除却仍不足。

00:11:59.136 --> 00:12:14.304
In suspected opioid poisoning, provide effective ventilation and use naloxone under the actual pathway. An incomplete wake-up response can reflect co-exposure; repeated medication is not a substitute for giving a needed breath.
疑阿片中毒应有效通气，按真实路径用纳洛酮。未完全醒可与混合暴露有关，反复给药不能代替必需通气。

00:12:14.304 --> 00:12:26.136
The goal is adequate breathing with ongoing assessment. Do not improvise a benzodiazepine antidote or conclude that a brief improvement makes recurrence and other pathology impossible.
目标是足够呼吸及持续评估，不能自创苯二氮䓬解药，也不能认为短暂改善后不可能再发或有其他病因。

00:12:26.136 --> 00:12:39.072
Poisoning and withdrawal are not opposite labels that can be assigned from agitation alone. Determine exposure and timing, assess physiology and consider mixed substances and other illnesses.
中毒与戒断不能仅凭激越就贴相反标签。须查暴露时序、评生理，并考虑混合物质及其他疾病。

00:12:39.072 --> 00:12:54.720
Opioid withdrawal commonly includes yawning, sweating, rhinorrhea, pain and gastrointestinal symptoms. Significant illness, dehydration, pregnancy or another substance withdrawal may change the risk and the needed care.
阿片戒断常有打哈欠、出汗、流鼻水、痛及胃肠症状；合并重病、脱水、妊娠或其他物质戒断，可改变风险及照护。

00:12:54.720 --> 00:13:07.728
COWS is not an overdose meter and should not be repurposed as an isolated stimulant-withdrawal scale. CIWA-Ar is an alcohol-withdrawal assessment, not a universal benzodiazepine withdrawal tool.
COWS不是过量计，也不能改作单纯兴奋剂戒断表；CIWA-Ar属酒精戒断，不是通用苯二氮䓬戒断工具。

00:13:07.728 --> 00:13:19.152
A score supports a defined assessment in an appropriate patient. It never overrides an immediate airway threat or creates permission to start an unauthorized medication regimen.
评分在合适患者中支持特定评估，不能凌驾即时气道威胁，也不会创造启动未获准药物方案的权限。

00:13:19.152 --> 00:13:34.512
Tolerance and physical dependence are not automatically opioid use disorder. OUD is a clinical pattern involving impaired control and significant harm or dysfunction, not a diagnosis made from housing status or appearance.
耐受及躯体依赖不自动等于阿片使用障碍。后者涉及控制受损及重要损害或功能异常，不能用住房或外貌诊断。

00:13:34.512 --> 00:13:49.824
Naloxone reversal addresses an acute threat. Longer-term treatment can include methadone, buprenorphine and other appropriate options. Naltrexone is a different drug and purpose; do not confuse similar names.
纳洛酮逆转处理急性威胁，长期治疗可包括美沙酮、丁丙诺啡及其他适合选择；纳曲酮是另一药及目的，不能因近名混淆。

00:13:49.824 --> 00:14:04.464
BC treatment resources and their updates guide access and clinical selection. Withdrawal management alone is not a prerequisite for ongoing treatment, and psychosocial support should not be used as a barrier to receiving medication.
BC治疗资源及更新指导获取及临床选择，单独戒断处理不是持续治疗前提，心理社会支持不应成为获得药物的障碍。

00:14:04.464 --> 00:14:19.320
Discuss recurrence, loss of tolerance, the unpredictable supply, naloxone access and safer-use support respectfully. Ask what the person wants and provide a realistic connection instead of demanding abstinence before offering help.
应尊重讨论再发、耐受下降、供应不可预测、纳洛酮可及及更安全支持，问患者目标并给现实连接，不先要求戒绝才帮助。

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:33.408
The innovations reading compares therapies with very different mechanisms and preparation. TMS is not ECT, and neither is a procedure to reconstruct from a summary or use as a PCP treatment option.
创新阅读比较机制准备很不同的治疗。TMS不等于ECT，两者都不能按摘要自行重建，也不是PCP可自行选的治疗。

00:14:33.408 --> 00:14:47.712
ECT requires individualized specialist screening, consent, anesthesia planning and recovery assessment. Avoid universal fasting rules or automatic exclusions based on one textbook sentence.
ECT需个体化专科筛查、同意、麻醉计划及恢复评估，不能从教材一句话推统一禁食或自动排除。

00:14:47.712 --> 00:15:02.064
For esketamine, the checked U.S. label requires at least two hours of monitoring and a stability assessment before leaving. A per-device amount is not the total regimen, and symptom improvement does not prove prevention of suicide.
艾司氯胺酮已核美国标签需至少2小时监测及离院前稳定评估；每器械量不是总方案，症状改善不证明预防自杀。

00:15:02.064 --> 00:15:15.792
Digital and remote care still need evidence, suitable access, privacy and a practical emergency plan. A technology label does not remove clinical risk or make a U.S. privacy declaration sufficient for BC.
数字远程照护仍需证据、适当可及、隐私及可行紧急计划。科技标签不会消除风险，美国隐私声明也不足以代表BC。

00:15:15.792 --> 00:15:29.976
Follow air from nose or mouth through pharynx, larynx, trachea and branching bronchi. Terminal bronchioles end the conducting zone; respiratory bronchioles begin the region where gas exchange becomes possible.
沿鼻口、咽喉、气管及分支支气管追空气。终末细支气管结束传导区，呼吸性细支气管开始可交换区域。

00:15:29.976 --> 00:15:44.808
Mucus, cilia and coordinated laryngeal protection reduce contamination but do not make aspiration impossible. The epiglottis helps protect the laryngeal entrance, not closes an opening from the esophagus.
黏液、纤毛及喉部协调保护减少污染，却不能保证不误吸。会厌保护喉入口，不是关闭来自食管的开口。

00:15:44.808 --> 00:15:58.656
Type One alveolar cells provide much of the thin exchange surface. Type Two cells produce surfactant at the inner air-liquid interface, helping reduce surface tension; macrophages contribute to defense.
Ⅰ型肺泡细胞提供大部分薄交换表面，Ⅱ型在内部气液界面产生表面活性物质以减表面张力，巨噬细胞参与防御。

00:15:58.656 --> 00:16:12.120
The surface must also receive ventilation and perfusion. Naming an alveolus is useful when you can explain why blocked airflow, fluid, lost surface or poor flow can impair the whole exchange chain.
表面还需通气及灌注。只有能解释梗阻、液体、表面损失或低流量如何破坏交换链，背出肺泡名称才有用。

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:25.344
Diaphragm and chest movement create pressure changes. Compliance describes volume change for pressure change; recoil is the tendency to return. They are related but not the same property.
膈及胸动产生压变化。顺应性是单位压变化的容积变化，回缩是恢复趋势，两者有关但不同。

00:16:25.344 --> 00:16:38.760
Rapid shallow breaths may provide inadequate alveolar ventilation. Hyperventilation means ventilation exceeds metabolic carbon dioxide production, not simply a high respiratory rate.
快速浅呼吸可肺泡通气不足。过度通气指通气超过代谢CO2生成，不只是次数高。

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:54.864
A normal saturation does not measure total oxygen content, tissue flow or carbon dioxide removal. Likewise, a normal blood pressure does not prove adequate microcirculation. Interpret the chain, not one reassuring number.
正常饱和度不测全部氧含量、组织流量或CO2清除，正常血压也不证明微循环足够。应解释整链，不只一个好数字。

00:16:54.864 --> 00:17:08.184
An exhausted person who becomes quiet and slow may be failing. Do not use a paper bag or suppress breathing on an assumed anxiety diagnosis; assess and support the actual physiological problem.
疲竭者安静变慢可在衰竭。不能因假定焦虑用纸袋或压制呼吸，要评估支持真实生理问题。

00:17:08.184 --> 00:17:25.728
An adult has taken an extra sedative and may also have used an opioid. Breaths are shallow at five per minute and responses are brief. Oxygen saturation is ninety-six percent after oxygen was applied. Pause and decide whether this is reassuring.
成人多服镇静物，也可能用过阿片，浅呼吸每分钟5次、仅简短反应，给氧后血氧96%。暂停判断这是否能放心。

00:17:25.728 --> 00:17:42.384
It is not reassuring. Open and assess the airway, clear obstruction or secretions as needed and provide effective ventilatory support under the trained pathway. Recheck chest movement, air entry and circulation while obtaining the exposure history.
不能放心。按受训路径开放评估气道、按需清梗阻分泌物并有效支持通气，查胸动气流循环，同时取得暴露史。

00:17:42.384 --> 00:17:58.656
If the opioid pathway applies, use its actual naloxone product and reassessment plan without delaying a breath. Record the oxygen device, dose actually delivered, time and response; do not invent a benzodiazepine reversal order.
若适用阿片路径，用真实纳洛酮产品及复评方案，但不延误通气。记录氧装置、实际给量、时间反应，不自创苯二氮䓬逆转医嘱。

00:17:58.656 --> 00:18:12.048
As awareness improves, explain continuing risks and reassess decision-making capacity. A briefly normal conversation does not by itself establish a safe discharge or an informed refusal.
意识改善后解释持续风险并重评决定能力。短暂正常交谈，本身不代表可安全离开或拒绝已知情。

00:18:12.048 --> 00:18:54.336
Correct the classification before interpreting the patient. Table 4.2 places lamotrigine among second-generation antipsychotics, but it is an antiseizure medicine also used for bipolar-I maintenance, not an antipsychotic. Nor are lithium, valproate, carbamazepine and lamotrigine one interchangeable voltage-channel-blocker mechanism. The paragraph also confuses 5HT with 5-hydroxytryptophan/dopamine: 5HT means serotonin, whereas 5-HTP is its precursor. A drug name, receptor and indication must be checked separately rather than inherited from a faulty table heading.
解释患者前先纠正分类。表4.2把拉莫三嗪放入第二代抗精神病药，但它是抗癫痫药，也用于双相I型维持治疗，不是抗精神病药。锂、丙戊酸、卡马西平和拉莫三嗪也不是可以互换的同一种电压通道阻断机制。正文还把5HT与5-羟色氨酸或多巴胺混淆：5HT是血清素，即5-羟色胺；5-HTP才是其前体。药名、受体和适应证应分别核实，不能从错误表头一路推导。

00:18:54.336 --> 00:19:32.136
Smoking history can change a medication story even when the tablet dose is unchanged. Tobacco smoke can induce CYP1A2 and reduce clozapine exposure; stopping that exposure can allow levels and adverse effects to rise. The medication does not contain the metabolic enzyme, as the textbook sentence implies. Ask about recent smoking changes, admission to a smoke-free setting, new sedation, dizziness and other symptoms, then communicate the change for clinician review. Do not tell the patient to resume smoking or independently recalculate the prescription.
即使片剂剂量没变，吸烟史也会改变用药经过。烟草烟雾可诱导CYP1A2，减少氯氮平暴露；停止这一暴露后，药物水平及不良效应可能上升。不是像教材句子暗示的那样，药物自身装有代谢酶。应问近期吸烟改变、是否进入无烟环境、新镇静、头晕及其他症状，并交代给临床人员评估；不能叫患者重新吸烟，也不能自行重算处方。

00:19:32.136 --> 00:20:09.144
Use the source timing windows as history clues, not diagnostic cutoffs. Dystonia often begins within hours to days after starting/increasing an antipsychotic, akathisia and parkinsonian features may emerge over the first weeks, and tardive movements often follow months or years. Ask about recent injections, dose changes and medicines removed as well as newly added. A distressed patient who cannot sit still may be describing a drug effect; a rigid jaw or tongue problem can threaten the airway and deserves immediate primary assessment.
把来源时间窗当问史线索，不当确诊界线。急性肌张力障碍常在开始或增加抗精神病药后数小时至数天出现；静坐不能及帕金森样表现可在最初数周出现；迟发性不自主运动常在数月或数年后出现。除新加药，还应问近期注射、加量及停掉的药。痛苦且坐不住可能是在描述药物影响；下颌强直或舌部问题可威胁气道，需立即初评。

00:20:09.144 --> 00:20:44.808
Original six-step application: notice the medication change and new jaw/voice abnormality; connect the timing and physical observations without assuming a psychiatric cause; prioritize airway risk; choose authorized support and early help; carry out and document those actions; then evaluate the actual response and revise the plan. The reading's clinic example waits an hour for a later documented review, but that is not permission to postpone reassessment of an acute airway threat. Use teach-back and the patient's concerns when discussing the next steps.
原创六步应用：发现用药改变及新下颌或声音异常；把时间与身体观察相连，不先认定精神原因；优先气道风险；选择获准支持并尽早求援；实施并记录；再评估实际反应、修订计划。阅读的门诊例子在一小时后记后续复评，不代表可推迟急性气道威胁的复查。讨论下一步时应用复述确认，也听患者的顾虑。

00:20:44.808 --> 00:21:33.456
For the source injection comparison, intradermal delivery targets the dermis at about 10-15 degrees; subcutaneous delivery targets fatty tissue at 45-90 degrees; intramuscular delivery targets muscle at 90 degrees. Its example needle ranges are respectively 25-27 gauge and one-quarter to one-half inch, 25-30 gauge and three-eighths to five-eighths inch, and 20-25 gauge and five-eighths to one-and-a-half inches. These are textbook examples, not a universal age/size selection rule. Match tissue depth, medicine, device and the actual approved procedure; neither a blanket pediatric length nor routine aspiration for every IM product is justified.
比较教材注射途径：皮内目标是真皮，约10至15度；皮下目标是脂肪组织，45至90度；肌注目标是肌肉，90度。书中示例针号和长度依次为25至27G、四分之一至二分之一英寸；25至30G、八分之三至八分之五英寸；20至25G、八分之五至一又二分之一英寸。这些是教材示例，不是所有年龄体型通用选择规则。应按组织深度、药物、装置及实际获准流程匹配；不能统一给儿科一种针长，也不能规定所有肌注产品常规回抽。

00:21:33.456 --> 00:22:12.240
Read the three IM-site drawings by landmarks rather than by a general body-region name. The deltoid site is located relative to the acromion and surrounding structures; vastus lateralis uses the outer middle third of the thigh, not the anterior rectus femoris; the ventrogluteal site uses the greater trochanter, anterior superior iliac spine and iliac crest. A buttock label is not permission to choose a dorsogluteal site. Practise identifying the actual landmarks, appropriate tissue and local exclusions with the instructor before practising the authorized injection sequence.
读三幅肌注部位图要认骨性标志，不能只背身体区域名。三角肌部位须结合肩峰及周边结构定位；股外侧肌在大腿外侧中三分之一，不是前面的股直肌；腹侧臀肌定位结合大转子、髂前上棘及髂嵴。“臀部”二字不允许自行改选背侧臀肌。应先与教师练习识别真实标志、适当组织及局部排除情况，再练获准注射顺序。

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:52.272
The assigned printed 676 already begins Advocacy, section 16.4. Its opening objectives and narrative connect advocacy to speaking up for patient needs and rights, helping the person obtain understandable information and appropriate services, and supporting professional standards. Advocacy means helping the patient voice their own preferences, not replacing those preferences with the clinician's choice. Patient-rights statements and nursing professional-rights lists are important ethical/organizational tools but are not all independently enacted BC statutes or authority to expand PCP scope.
指定印刷676页已经开始16.4“倡导”。开头目标及正文把倡导连到为患者需要和权利发声，帮助取得可理解信息及适当服务，并支持专业标准。倡导是帮助患者表达自身偏好，不是用临床人员选择取代它。患者权利声明及护理专业权利清单是重要伦理或机构工具，却不全都是独立颁布的BC法律，也不扩张PCP范围。

00:22:52.272 --> 00:23:46.032
Keep adult-consent principles separate from the authority of a particular practitioner. The BC adult consent Act defines a statutory provider through prescribed legislation; Consent Regulation section 3 names the Health Professions and Occupations Act and Social Workers Act, not the Emergency Health Services Act. Therefore do not assign an EMA every hospital-provider or temporary-substitute-decision-maker power simply by citing that Act. Use the actual EMA role, current service consent/refusal pathway and consultation. Infants Act section 17 separately requires explanation, understanding of nature/consequences and reasonably foreseeable benefits/risks, and reasonable efforts to conclude the care is in the young person's best interests; it is not a fixed birthday or a signature-only rule.
成人同意原则与某位从业者真实权限要分开。BC成人同意法通过指定法律界定法定提供者；《Consent Regulation》第3条列《Health Professions and Occupations Act》及《Social Workers Act》，不是《Emergency Health Services Act》。因此不能仅引用成人法，就赋予EMA所有医院提供者或临时替代决策者的权力。应按真实EMA角色、当前服务同意拒绝路径及咨询办理。《Infants Act》第17条另外要求作解释，理解性质、后果及合理可预见的利益风险，并作合理努力后认定照护符合该年轻人的最佳利益；不是固定生日或只签名规则。

00:23:46.032 --> 00:24:33.264
BC safeguarding routes are not interchangeable. CFCSA section 14 requires prompt reporting when there is reason to believe a child needs protection under section 13; the specified Indigenous-authority route has its own confirmation requirement. Merely telling a supervisor is not the statutory report. Adult Guardianship Act section 46 says a person may report to a designated agency where the section 44 circumstances apply; it is not a blanket mandatory report of every adult concern, and capable adult choices remain relevant. Other specific duties can still apply. Observe objectively, communicate privately and use the actual applicable route rather than promise secrecy or broadcast an allegation.
BC保护报告路径不能互换。CFCSA第14条要求，有理由相信儿童处于第13条需保护情形时迅速报告；特定原住民机构路径还有确认要求。只告诉主管不等于法定报告。《Adult Guardianship Act》第46条对第44条情形写的是可向指定机构报告，不是所有成人疑虑一律强制报告；有能力成人的选择仍重要。其他特定义务仍可适用。应客观观察、私下沟通并采用真实适用路径，不能保证绝对保密，也不能广播指控。

00:24:33.264 --> 00:25:11.328
The lawsuit diagram is a process map: a claim is filed and served, a response is made, evidence is exchanged in discovery, and the matter may settle or proceed to trial and judgment. The source example includes a fourteen-day response step; that is not a BC deadline taught by this course. A claim is not a finding of negligence, and a settlement is not automatically an admission. When a complaint or legal notice arrives, preserve records and follow the actual employer, insurer and professional process rather than altering old notes or contacting witnesses to align accounts.
诉讼图展示流程：提出并送达请求、作出回应、在证据开示中交换证据，之后可能和解或进入审理及判决。来源示例有十四天回应步骤，本课不把它当BC期限。提出索赔不等于已经认定过失，和解也不自动等于承认。收到投诉或法律通知，应保留记录并遵真实雇主、保险及专业流程，不能改旧病历或联系证人统一说法。

00:25:11.328 --> 00:25:54.816
Trace the RAAS figure in order: the kidney releases renin, which acts on liver-derived angiotensinogen to form angiotensin I; ACE helps form angiotensin II. Pulmonary vascular endothelium is an important site, not the only place ACE exists. Angiotensin II supports vasoconstriction and adrenal aldosterone release; aldosterone promotes sodium retention with water following. The diagram also shows ADH-related water reabsorption. These mechanisms link lungs, kidneys, vessels and volume regulation over time; they do not establish that one BP reading proves adequate perfusion or authorize a drug or fluid amount.
按顺序读RAAS图：肾释放肾素，作用于肝来源血管紧张素原，形成血管紧张素Ⅰ；ACE帮助生成Ⅱ。肺血管内皮是重要部位，但不是ACE唯一所在。血管紧张素Ⅱ促血管收缩及肾上腺醛固酮释放；醛固酮促钠潴留，水随之保留。图还示ADH相关水重吸收。这些机制把肺、肾、血管与容量调节连起来，并随时间作用；不能据一个血压认定灌注足够，也不能由此授权某药或补液量。

00:25:54.816 --> 00:26:36.960
The incentive spirometer picture illustrates a slow deep inspiration, not blowing out through a peak-flow meter. With the prescribed device and individual goal, the person inhales steadily, watches the volume/feedback marker and demonstrates the technique back. Check pain, understanding, cognition, hearing and the ability to use the mouthpiece; a generic volume or schedule is not suitable for everyone. Incentive spirometry supports a prescribed lung-expansion plan. It is not assisted ventilation, CPAP or a diagnostic pulmonary-function result, and must not delay help for an acutely failing patient.
激励肺量计图片示慢而深的吸气，不是像峰流速计那样往外吹。按所开装置及个体目标，患者平稳吸气、观察容积或反馈标记，再演示确认技术。须查疼痛、理解、认知、听力及能否使用咬嘴；统一容积或频次不适合所有人。它服务于规定肺扩张计划，不是辅助通气、CPAP或诊断肺功能结果，也不能延误急性衰竭患者求援。

00:26:36.960 --> 00:27:23.112
Use the arterial-gas table as a recognition exercise, not a treatment order: the source pairs respiratory alkalosis with arterial pH above 7.45 and PaCO2 below 35 mmHg, and respiratory acidosis with pH below 7.35 and PaCO2 above 45 mmHg. Compensation and mixed disorders can change the pattern, so interpret all available gases and the actual patient. PaCO2 is arterial carbon dioxide pressure, not oxygen saturation; PaO2 is arterial oxygen pressure, not the SpO2 display. A fast respiratory rate does not by itself tell you any of these values.
动脉血气表用于识别练习，不是治疗令：来源把呼吸性碱中毒配为动脉pH大于7.45、PaCO2小于35mmHg，把呼吸性酸中毒配为pH小于7.35、PaCO2大于45mmHg。代偿及混合紊乱会改变模式，需结合全部可得血气及患者。PaCO2是动脉二氧化碳分压，不是血氧饱和度；PaO2是动脉氧分压，也不是SpO2屏幕读数。仅呼吸快不能推出任何这些值。

00:27:23.112 --> 00:28:02.928
The assigned printed 792 already opens 19.2 Cardiovascular System. Its introductory framework connects the pump, circulating volume and vessels to tissue perfusion, then locates the heart in the mediastinum and begins describing the great vessels. Use this opening to connect breathing with circulation: oxygen reaching alveoli still needs blood flow, hemoglobin and a functioning pump to reach tissues. The assignment ends mid-description; it does not assign the entire following cardiovascular section, and a normal BP alone cannot certify the whole delivery system.
指定印刷792页已经开始19.2“心血管系统”。开头框架把泵、循环容量及血管连到组织灌注，随后定位心脏在纵隔并开始描述大血管。应用开头把呼吸与循环相连：氧到肺泡后还需血流、血红蛋白及有效泵送才能到组织。指定范围在描述中途结束，不等于把后续整节心血管都指定了；单个正常血压也不能认证整个输送系统。

00:28:02.928 --> 00:28:42.120
The assigned chapter summary connects critical thinking to clinical judgment. Use the six CJMM actions as a loop: recognize cues, analyze them, prioritize hypotheses, generate solutions, take action and evaluate outcomes. A hypothesis remains provisional. For example, a person unable to finish a sentence needs an immediate breathing assessment while the team gathers history; do not choose a familiar diagnosis and stop noticing contradictory findings. Record relevant positive and genuinely assessed negative findings, then explain how the repeated assessment changes the plan.
指定章总结把批判思考连到临床判断。把CJMM六步当循环：识别线索、分析、排列假设优先级、形成方案、行动及评价结果。假设仍是暂定。例如说不完一句话者需立即评估呼吸，同时团队收集病史；不能选熟悉诊断后就不再注意矛盾发现。记录相关阳性及真正评过的阴性，再解释复评怎样改变计划。

00:28:42.120 --> 00:29:23.016
Check units before accepting a charted number. The source abdominal chart pairs 89.3 degrees Fahrenheit with 38.5 degrees Celsius, but they are not equivalent: 38.5 Celsius is 101.3 Fahrenheit, while 89.3 Fahrenheit is about 31.8 Celsius. The mismatch is a reason to verify the original measurement, unit, time and patient, not to choose the number that fits a preferred diagnosis. Apply the same discipline to drug strength, laboratory units and times. This is a data-quality lesson, not an answer to the source worked-case questions.
接纳病历数字前先核单位。来源腹部病历把89.3华氏度与38.5摄氏度并列，但两者不等：38.5摄氏等于101.3华氏，89.3华氏约31.8摄氏。冲突提示要核原始测量、单位、时间及患者，不是挑符合预想诊断的数。同样纪律应用于药物含量、化验单位及时间。这是资料质量教学，不是来源案例题答案。

00:29:23.016 --> 00:29:59.928
Read the actual Figure 7.9 rather than its erroneous caption. Although labelled a pain-treatment agreement, the displayed sheet explains U.S. Prescription Drug Monitoring Programs: databases collect controlled-substance prescription information, can reveal duplicate therapy or interactions, and require appropriate privacy/access controls. A monitoring database and a shared treatment agreement are different tools. Neither its U.S. access rules nor its phone numbers become BC instructions, and the presence of a prescription record does not prove what the patient took today.
要读实际图7.9，不盲信错误图注。虽然标为疼痛治疗协议，显示的纸页其实解释美国处方药监测项目：数据库收集受控药处方资料，可发现重复治疗或相互作用，并需适当隐私及权限控制。监测数据库与共同治疗协议是不同工具。其美国访问规则及电话号码都不变成BC指令，有处方记录也不证明患者今天实际吃了什么。

00:29:59.928 --> 00:30:43.896
Correct the SUD treatment comparison: methadone is an opioid agonist, buprenorphine a partial agonist, and naltrexone an antagonist. Naltrexone is not simply a weaker opioid used to wean a person off a stronger one; starting it after recent opioid exposure can precipitate severe withdrawal. Likewise, physical dependence is physiologic adaptation with withdrawal risk after reduction, not by itself proof of OUD or a moral failing. Ask what medicine is actually used and when it was last taken; continuing treatment and acute pain both deserve an individualized clinician plan. No initiation, stopping, taper or dose is supplied here.
纠正物质使用障碍治疗比较：美沙酮是阿片激动药，丁丙诺啡是部分激动药，纳曲酮是拮抗药。纳曲酮不是用来把强阿片减掉的“较弱阿片”；近期用过阿片后启用可诱发严重戒断。同样，躯体依赖是减量后有戒断风险的生理适应，本身不证明OUD或品德问题。应问实际用药及末次时间；持续治疗及急性疼痛都需要个体化临床计划。本段不给启用、停药、减量或剂量。

00:30:43.896 --> 00:31:23.808
Follow the auscultation figure by comparing matching levels side to side, moving from upper to lower accessible fields on the front and back when safe; avoid listening through bone or assuming a numbered dot samples an entire lobe. Bronchial sounds are normally louder and higher pitched centrally, bronchovesicular sounds intermediate over larger bronchi, and vesicular sounds softer over peripheral fields. Document site, phase, symmetry and intensity, not simply lungs clear. A patient unable to tolerate repositioning needs adapted assessment and immediate support, not completion of every dot first.
按听诊图在同水平双侧比较，安全时由上至下检查前后可接近肺野；不要隔骨头听，也不要以为一个编号点就代表整叶。正常中央支气管音较响高，较大支气管处支气管肺泡音居中，周边肺野肺泡音较柔。记录部位、时相、对称及强弱，不只写“两肺清”。无法耐受换位者需调整检查并即时支持，不是先点完所有点。

00:31:23.808 --> 00:32:09.552
Local pulmonary vascular responses can partly redirect flow away from poorly ventilated regions, but this does not guarantee adequate total gas exchange. Air reaching an alveolus without usable blood flow and blood passing a poorly ventilated region are different mismatch patterns. Connect the source table to separate mechanisms: narrowing restricts airflow, reduced expansion/drive limits ventilation, filling/collapse impairs exchange, low hemoglobin reduces carrying capacity, and a vascular obstruction limits perfusion. Several can coexist, so reassess both breathing and circulation instead of assigning every abnormal saturation the same explanation.
局部肺血管反应可部分把血流从通气差区域引开，但不保证总体交换足够。空气到肺泡却无可用血流，与血流经过通气差区域，是不同失配模式。把来源表连到不同机制：狭窄限气流，扩张或驱动少限通气，填充塌陷损交换，低血红蛋白降携氧，血管阻塞限灌注。多项可并存，所以要复评呼吸及循环，不能给所有异常血氧同一解释。

00:32:09.552 --> 00:32:54.120
Read the concentration-time plot by its axes and thresholds. Time is horizontal; plasma concentration is vertical. An illustrative curve crosses an example minimum effective concentration, reaches a peak and later falls below that threshold. The therapeutic window is the concentration band between desired and adverse-response thresholds, not the length of time between crossings and not a therapeutic-index ratio. The source mixes Drug Effect with Cp and describes peak effect as if it always equalled peak blood level; real effects can lag. Use the actual person, exposure and response rather than predicting a safe repeat dose or discharge time from this schematic.
读浓度时间图先看坐标和阈值：横轴时间，纵轴血浆浓度。示意曲线越过某个最低有效浓度、到峰值、后来再降至其下。治疗窗是期望反应与不良反应阈值间的浓度带，不是两次越线之间的时长，也不是治疗指数比值。来源把Drug Effect与Cp混写，并把效应峰值当总等于血药峰值；真实效应可滞后。应看真实患者、暴露及反应，不能由示意图预测安全重复给药或离院时间。

00:32:54.120 --> 00:33:44.304
Use the actual label illustrations to separate content, concentration and dose. The tablet label gives 125 mcg, also written 0.125 mg, per tablet. The illustrated injection contains 100 mcg in 2 mL, equivalent to 50 mcg/mL; the vial total is not the amount per millilitre. One milligram equals one thousand micrograms. Generic name, strength, route/form, expiry, single-dose designation and manufacturer serve different checks. A controlled-substance symbol belongs to its jurisdiction and does not establish BC scheduling or permission. These are label-reading examples, not instructions to administer digoxin or fentanyl.
用实际标签图区分总含量、浓度及剂量。片剂标签为每片125微克，也写0.125毫克。注射剂图为2毫升共100微克，即每毫升50微克；整瓶总量不是每毫升药量。1毫克等于1000微克。通用名、含量、途径剂型、效期、单次用标示及制造商分别服务不同核查。受控药标志属于其司法地区，不证明BC分类或给药许可。这是读标签例子，不是地高辛或芬太尼给药指令。

00:33:44.304 --> 00:34:28.056
Ephedrine and epinephrine are not interchangeable names or products. Both have adrenergic effects beyond airway smooth muscle, so pulse, rhythm, blood pressure and interacting sympathomimetic/MAOI exposure matter. The source ephedrine table calls intermittent asthma both an indication and a contraindication; do not convert that contradiction into a patient rule. Its epinephrine table also gives volumes without a clear concentration in the sentence. Use the actual current indication, product concentration, route and local protocol. An inhaled product or oral ephedrine example is not a replacement for the anaphylaxis IM pathway.
麻黄碱与肾上腺素不是可互换的名字或产品。两者肾上腺素能作用都不只气道平滑肌，因此脉搏节律、血压及其他拟交感或MAOI暴露重要。来源麻黄碱表把间歇性哮喘同时列适应证和禁忌，不能把矛盾变患者规则。肾上腺素表的句子还给体积却未清楚给浓度。应按真实当前适应证、产品浓度、途径及本地流程。吸入产品或口服麻黄碱示例，不替代过敏性休克肌注路径。

00:34:28.056 --> 00:35:15.360
The last assigned printed697already begins25.2and includes its objectives, inflammation illustration and first drug table. Beclomethasone is the inhaled corticosteroid example, while prednisone is an oral systemic example; they are not interchangeable formulations or an immediate bronchodilator. The figure contrasts airway wall inflammation, mucus and narrowed lumen with an unobstructed example. Corticosteroids address inflammation on the relevant treatment timescale, not rescue ventilation. The full following steroid discussion is outside this page span, and neither inhaled steroids for every COPD patient nor the wide oral dose range is made a blanket instruction here.
最后指定印刷697页已开始25.2，含目标、炎症示意及首张药表。倍氯米松是吸入糖皮质激素例，泼尼松是口服全身用例；两者不是可互换剂型，也不是即时支扩药。图比较气道壁炎症、黏液及管腔变窄与通畅示例。糖皮质激素在相应治疗时间尺度处理炎症，不替代救援通气。后续完整激素讨论不在这段页内，本课也不把所有COPD患者都用吸入激素或表中宽泛口服剂量变成统一指令。

00:35:15.360 --> 00:36:01.656
Use the cardiovascular name stems as recognition prompts, then verify the real medicine: -pril commonly suggests an ACE inhibitor, -sartan an angiotensin-receptor blocker, -dipine a dihydropyridine calcium-channel blocker, -lol a beta blocker, -osin an alpha blocker and -dralazine the hydralazine vasodilator example. The source -ide examples include furosemide and hydrochlorothiazide, but -ide is far too broad to identify all diuretics. The -vastatin examples concern lipid-lowering drugs, not an immediate blood-pressure treatment. Knowing a class helps focus the exposure history; it supplies neither an indication nor a dose for this patient.
把心血管药名词干当识别提示，再核真实药：-pril常提示ACE抑制药，-sartan为血管紧张素受体阻断药，-dipine为二氢吡啶类钙通道阻断药，-lol为β阻断药，-osin为α阻断药，-dralazine举肼屈嗪血管扩张药。来源-ide举呋塞米及氢氯噻嗪，但-ide太宽，不能据此识别所有利尿药。-vastatin例子涉及降脂，不是即时降压治疗。认类别帮助聚焦暴露史，却不给这名患者创造适应证或剂量。

00:36:01.656 --> 00:36:42.216
Test the naming rule against exceptions. Aripiprazole is not a proton-pump inhibitor merely because its name ends in prazole. The source separates -statin examples such as cilastatin/pepstatin from lipid-lowering -vastatin examples. Its minaxolone entry refers to a steroid-structured anesthetic studied historically, not permission to classify it as an anti-inflammatory corticosteroid. A drug class may describe chemistry, mechanism or therapeutic use, which are different classification axes. Resolve the actual generic product and mechanism before using a suffix to explain the patient.
要用例外检验药名规则。阿立哌唑不会因为名字以prazole结尾就成为质子泵抑制药。来源把西司他丁或胃蛋白酶抑制剂等-statin例，与降脂-vastatin例分开。其米那索龙条目指历史研究的甾体结构麻醉药，不允许把它当抗炎糖皮质激素。药物分类可按化学结构、机制或治疗用途，这些是不同轴。解释患者前，要核真实通用产品及机制，不能只靠词尾。

00:36:42.216 --> 00:37:24.408
For nervous-system and symptom medicines, -azepam suggests the benzodiazepine examples, -barb- the barbiturates, -caine local-anesthetic examples, -axine the venlafaxine antidepressant example, -peridol and -peridone antipsychotic examples, and -pidem a hypnotic such as zolpidem. Do not assume every barbiturate is being used for seizures or every antidepressant for the same diagnosis. Ask about actual indication, recent changes, sedation, breathing and interactions. A shared naming fragment does not make two products interchangeable or prove that an observed behaviour is psychiatric.
神经及症状用药中，-azepam提示来源苯二氮䓬例，-barb-为巴比妥类，-caine举局麻药，-axine举文拉法辛抗抑郁药，-peridol及-peridone举抗精神病药，-pidem举唑吡坦等催眠药。不能认为所有巴比妥都用于惊厥，或每种抗抑郁药都治同一诊断。应问实际用途、近期改变、镇静、呼吸及相互作用。同一词干不使产品可互换，也不证明某种行为是精神原因。

00:37:24.408 --> 00:38:06.048
The anti-infective and other source stems include -cillin for penicillin-family beta-lactams, -cycline for tetracycline examples, -oxacin for fluoroquinolones, -conazole for antifungals and -vir for antiviral examples. Other recognition groups are -atadine antihistamines, -ac and -profen NSAID examples, -terol bronchodilators and the omeprazole -prazole proton-pump-inhibitor example. These cues help ask targeted questions about allergy, interactions and intended use. They do not determine infection type, rescue-versus-maintenance use or whether an unfamiliar same-ending medicine belongs to that class.
来源抗感染及其他词干包括：-cillin为青霉素类β内酰胺药，-cycline举四环素类，-oxacin举氟喹诺酮类，-conazole为抗真菌药，-vir举抗病毒药。其他识别组有-atadine抗组胺药，-ac及-profen举NSAID，-terol举支扩药，-prazole举奥美拉唑等质子泵抑制药。这些提示帮助针对过敏、相互作用及用途提问，不确定感染类型、救援或维持用途，也不保证陌生同词尾药属于同组。

00:38:06.048 --> 00:38:55.536
Original gravity-flow rehearsal: a simulation instruction specifies 180 mL over 60 minutes using a set labelled 20 gtt/mL. Calculate 180 mL times 20 gtt/mL divided by 60 minutes = 60 gtt/min. Reverse-check: 60 gtt/min times 60 minutes divided by 20 gtt/mL = 180 mL. A pump would express this example as 180 mL/hour, not 60 mL/hour. A different set factor changes the drop rate. This is unit practice, not a fluid order; verify the actual authorized amount, patient, access, delivery system and response.
原创重力流量排练：模拟指示为60分钟给180mL，输液器标20gtt/mL。180mL×20gtt/mL÷60min=60gtt/min。反查：60gtt/min×60min÷20gtt/mL=180mL。此例输注泵应表达180mL/h，不是60mL/h。换输液器滴系数，滴速就变。这是单位练习，不是补液医嘱，仍须核实际获准量、患者、通路、系统及反应。

00:38:55.536 --> 00:39:41.688
Original daily-dose rehearsal: an unnamed training medicine is ordered at 8 mg/kg/day for an 18 kg simulation patient, divided every 12 hours, with a training concentration of 24 mg/mL. Daily amount is 144 mg/day; two administrations per day give 72 mg/dose; 72 mg divided by 24 mg/mL gives 3 mL/dose. Reverse-check both the dose and the daily total. If the instruction were per kilogram per dose, this calculation would be different. No real pediatric drug, safe maximum or permission to administer has been supplied by this exercise.
原创每日剂量排练：无名训练药按18kg模拟患者8mg/kg/day开，每12小时分次，训练浓度24mg/mL。日量144mg/day，每日两次得到72mg/dose，72mg÷24mg/mL=3mL/dose。既反查每次，也反查每日总量。若指示改成每千克每次，计算就不同。练习没有提供真实儿科药、安全上限或给药权限。

00:39:41.688 --> 00:40:28.968
Compare the actual inhaler motions. A pressurized MDI coordinates a slow inhalation with actuation, with an appropriate spacer/valved chamber when indicated. A DPI needs adequate device-specific inspiratory effort; load or pierce its capsule only as instructed, exhale away, and never swallow an inhalation capsule. A soft-mist inhaler has its own preparation and dose-release sequence with a slow inhalation. Rinsing and spitting after an inhaled corticosteroid addresses local exposure, not a universal rule that every inhaler contains a steroid. Ask for return demonstration when stable; device preparation must not delay support for ineffective breaths.
比较真实吸入器动作：加压MDI配合缓慢吸气与揿药，适应时使用合适储雾罐或带阀腔。DPI需要足够且符合装置的吸气力量；只按说明装填或刺破胶囊，向装置外呼气，绝不能吞吸入胶囊。软雾装置有自己的准备及剂量释放顺序，并配缓慢吸气。吸入糖皮质激素后漱口吐出是处理局部暴露，不代表每种吸入器都含激素。稳定时请回演，准备装置不能延误无效呼吸的支持。

00:40:28.968 --> 00:41:07.488
The source sequence of bronchodilator, dornase alfa, airway clearance, inhaled antibiotic and steroid is a specific multi-treatment context, not an order to give every breathless person all five. Match each prescribed treatment to its purpose and the person's actual care plan. Bronchodilation, secretion modification, antimicrobial treatment and anti-inflammatory control solve different problems. Check what was already taken, whether the person can use the device and how the response changes the next action; do not turn the list into an automatic PCP treatment stack.
来源的支扩、阿法链道酶、清除气道分泌物、吸入抗生素及激素顺序，是特定多措施背景，不是让每个气促者都接受五项。每项处方要匹配目的及患者真实照护计划。支扩、改变分泌物、抗微生物及抗炎控制处理不同问题。要查已用什么、能否使用装置及反应怎样改变下一行动，不能把清单变PCP自动叠药。

00:41:07.488 --> 00:41:46.800
Read the drain photographs by system and purpose. Hemovac and Jackson-Pratt examples use a compressed reservoir to provide closed-system suction; a Penrose example allows passive drainage into a dressing. A pigtail describes a curled catheter shape, not by itself the destination, fluid or suction plan. The source notes emptying closed reservoirs around one-third to one-half full and measuring output, but a hospital shift schedule is not an EMS monitoring interval. Know what is connected, keep it secured and communicate the actual type, site and output trend before moving the patient.
按系统及目的读引流照片：Hemovac及Jackson-Pratt示例用压缩储液器产生封闭负压，Penrose示例被动引流到敷料。“猪尾”描述导管卷曲形状，本身不确定位置、液体或负压计划。来源提封闭储液器约三分之一至一半满时排空并量输出，但医院每班安排不是EMS监测间隔。移动患者前应知道连接物、保持固定，并交代真实类型、部位及输出趋势。

00:41:46.800 --> 00:42:33.792
Original integrated encounter: a postoperative adult has new drain leakage, increasing sleepiness after an extra home analgesic and very shallow breaths despite a reassuring saturation on oxygen. First assess/support the immediate airway and breathing threat, obtain help and reassess circulation; do not complete a dressing change before restoring effective breaths. Then reconcile the actual medicine, amount and timeline, describe the wound/device/output change and preserve the appropriate system during transfer. Handover should connect observations, actual actions and response, not diagnose every symptom from the drain or dismiss deterioration because a monitor number looks normal.
原创整合场景：术后成人引流部位新漏液，额外服家中镇痛药后越来越困，给氧血氧看似好，呼吸却很浅。先评估支持即时气道呼吸威胁、求援并复评循环，不能先换完敷料才恢复有效呼吸。随后核真实药、量及时序，描述伤口装置输出改变，转运时适当保护系统。交接要连观察、实际行动及反应，不能把所有症状都归引流管，也不能因监护数字好就否定恶化。

00:42:33.792 --> 00:43:26.472
Keep the source oxygen numbers with their setting. Checklist 42 mentions an expected saturation above 95%, a general treatment band of 92-98% and a low-start nasal-prong example. The historical flowchart instead branches at 88% or below versus 89-91%, with different initial nasal flows and five-minute reassessment. Table 5.6 discusses 88-92% for a known chronic-retention context. These are not one internally identical algorithm, a rule to wait five minutes during failure or a reason to start every critically ill person on low-flow prongs. Use the actual school/current BCEHS indication, device, target and exception pathway; treat ineffective ventilation as a different immediate problem.
来源氧疗数字须带场景。清单42提预期血氧大于95%、一般治疗带92至98%及低流量鼻导管起始示例；历史流程图却按88%及以下与89至91%分支，给不同起始鼻流量并五分钟复评；表5.6又讨论已知慢性潴留背景88至92%。它们不是完全一致的一套算法，不允许衰竭时等五分钟，也不要求所有危重者都先低流量鼻导管。应按真实学校及当前BCEHS适应证、装置、目标和例外路径，无效通气是另一即时问题。

00:43:26.472 --> 00:44:19.512
Distinguish the source oral Yankauer procedure from its flexible oropharyngeal-catheter procedure: they use different equipment, depth/asepsis considerations and monitoring. The actual 2018 copy also prints the unresolved portable 10-15 mmHg value beside a 100-150 mmHg wall-suction range; do not silently reinterpret the unit as kPa or transplant either number to every device/age/route. Use the school-trained method and verified device settings, clear the obstruction without prolonged suction or tissue trauma, and reassess between attempts. Worsening oxygenation, bleeding, distress or ineffective breaths calls for stopping/reassessment and appropriate support, not finishing a textbook sequence first.
要分清来源口腔Yankauer与柔性口咽导管吸引，两者器材、深度和无菌要求及监测不同。实际2018副本也把未解决的便携10至15mmHg与壁式100至150mmHg并列，不能悄悄把单位改成kPa，也不能套所有装置、年龄及途径。须按学校受训方法及核实装置设置清除阻塞，避免长吸或组织损伤，尝试间复评。氧合变坏、出血、窘迫或无效呼吸，需停止重评及适当支持，不是先做完教材顺序。

00:44:19.512 --> 00:45:03.384
The scheduled-medication table distinguishes locally defined time-critical medicines from other scheduled medicines: it gives a thirty-minute window for selected time-critical orders, one hour for some other repeated schedules and two hours for daily/weekly/monthly examples. This is a hospital scheduling framework, not a universal allowance to delay an emergency medicine or redefine PRN repeat limits. Clarify the actual order and current policy, then record the time actually administered. An electronic MAR checked by two people can still contain the same stale order; reconciliation must compare actual patient use and the authoritative current instruction.
定时药表区分机构定义的时效关键药与其他定时药，举部分关键医嘱三十分钟窗口、其他某些重复安排一小时、每日每周每月示例两小时。这是医院排程框架，不是统一允许推迟急救药，也不重写PRN重复上限。应澄清真实医嘱及当前政策，记实际给药时间。即使两人核过电子MAR，仍可能共用同一过期医嘱；核药需对比患者实际使用及权威当前指示。

00:45:03.384 --> 00:45:50.040
For a feeding-tube medicine, verify the tube type/destination, the approved placement check and the actual product/formulation before delivery. A whoosh, aspirate appearance or lack of distress alone does not prove initial NG placement; the NHS enduring standard uses a validated safe-range pH result or appropriate x-ray confirmation in its setting. Give suitable medicines separately and follow the individualized flush/feed plan. The book's 30/15/30 mL flush and feed-interruption examples are not universal pediatric or fluid-restricted instructions. Do not force resistance, mix everything into feed or use an uncertain tube merely because the syringe fits.
经喂养管给药前，核管型终点、获准位置核实及真实药物剂型。仅听注气声、看抽液外观或没有窘迫，不证明鼻胃管初次位置；NHS持续有效标准在其场景采用经验证安全范围pH或适当X线确认。合适药要分开给，按个体冲管及喂养计划。书中30、15、30mL冲管和停喂示例，不是所有儿科或限液通则。不能强推阻力、把药全混进喂养液，或仅因针筒接得上就用位置未明的管。

00:45:50.040 --> 00:46:03.168
Without notes, explain why a correct milligram calculation can still lead to unsafe care. Include the patient, indication, formulation, route, delivery and response in your answer.
不看笔记解释：毫克计算正确为何仍可不安全？答案须有患者、适应证、剂型、途径、送入及反应。

00:46:03.168 --> 00:46:15.072
Then distinguish opioid poisoning, opioid withdrawal and ongoing opioid use disorder treatment. Name what COWS does, what it does not do and why naloxone is not naltrexone.
再区分阿片中毒、戒断及持续使用障碍治疗。说清COWS用途与非用途，以及纳洛酮为何不等于纳曲酮。

00:46:15.072 --> 00:46:25.584
Explain two medication-related red flags that should not be dismissed as psychiatric behaviour, and one respiratory finding that overrides a normal saturation display.
解释两项不能用精神行为敷衍的药物红旗，以及一项足以推翻正常血氧显示的呼吸发现。

00:46:25.584 --> 00:46:40.104
Finally open the book-specific bilingual guides and work through the original retrieval prompts. Keep the exact school edition and unrecovered activities visible in the coverage record rather than marking them complete by familiarity.
最后打开各教材双语讲解，完成原创提取。准确学校版及未取得活动应保留在覆盖记录，不能因为熟悉就标完成。
